Q3. Will this code compile?

interface A {
    void show();
}

class B implements A {

    void show() {
        System.out.println("Hello");
    }
}

A. Yes, it compiles successfully
B. No, show() must be public
C. No, show() must be protected
D. Runtime error

ANSWER: B
OUTPUT: Compile-time error.

REASON:
Interface methods are public by default.
The implementing method cannot reduce visibility from public to
package-private.


