Q5. Find the problem:

interface Payment {
    void pay();
}

class UPI implements Payment {

    public void payment() {
        System.out.println("UPI");
    }
}

A. Nothing is wrong
B. Method name doesn't match the interface
C. Method should be private
D. Interface cannot be implemented

ANSWER: B
OUTPUT: Compile-time error.

REASON:
The interface requires pay(), but the class defines payment().
Therefore UPI does not implement the required method.


