Q17. Predict the output:

interface Animal {
    void sound();
}

class Dog implements Animal {
    public void sound() {
        System.out.println("Dog");
    }
}

class Cat implements Animal {
    public void sound() {
        System.out.println("Cat");
    }
}

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Animal a = new Dog();
        a = new Cat();

        a.sound();
    }
}

A. Dog
B. Cat
C. Dog and Cat
D. Compile-time error

ANSWER: B
OUTPUT:
Cat

REASON:
The second assignment replaces the reference:

a = new Cat();

So at runtime, a points to Cat.


