Q22. What happens?

interface Vehicle {
    void start();
}

class Car implements Vehicle {

    public void start() {
        System.out.println("Car");
    }

    public void drive() {
        System.out.println("Drive");
    }
}

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Vehicle v = new Car();

        v.drive();
    }
}

A. Prints Drive
B. Compile-time error
C. Runtime error
D. Prints Car

ANSWER: B
OUTPUT:
Compile-time error.

REASON:
Reference type is Vehicle.

Vehicle v = new Car();

The Vehicle interface does not contain drive().
Therefore v.drive() is not accessible.


