Q23. What change is required?

interface A {
    void show();
}

class B implements A {

    private void show() {
        System.out.println("Hello");
    }
}

A. Change private to public
B. Change private to protected
C. Change void to static void
D. No change required

ANSWER: A
OUTPUT:
Change private to public.

Correct:

public void show() {
    System.out.println("Hello");
}

REASON:
An interface method is public.
An implementing method cannot have weaker visibility.


