Q25. FINAL INTERVIEW-LEVEL QUESTION

interface A {
    default void show() {
        System.out.println("A");
    }
}

interface B extends A {
    default void show() {
        System.out.println("B");
    }
}

class C implements B {
}

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        A obj = new C();
        obj.show();
    }
}

A. A
B. B
C. Compile-time error
D. Runtime error

ANSWER: B
OUTPUT:
B

REASON:

A
 ↓
B  → overrides A.show()
 ↓
C  → inherits B.show()

Even though the reference is:

A obj

the actual object is C, and C inherits B's implementation.

Therefore:

B
